# Excludes paths from eas-cli's shallow-clone tarball when uploading to
# EAS Build. Works like .gitignore. Critical on Replit because eas-cli
# walks UP from apps/mobile to the workspace root when bundling, and the
# Replit shell drops gigabytes of cache + sandbox state there that has no
# business being in a mobile build context.
#
# Three failure modes this prevents (all observed during S0 init):
#   1. EACCES rmdir on .cache/dotslash/.../React Native DevTools-linux-x64
#      — dotslash unpacks binaries with locked perms; cleanup fails.
#   2. Unknown system error -122 (filesystem quota) copying the entire
#      pnpm content-addressable store — millions of files, copy explodes.
#   3. Replit-specific config (.replit, .config/, .local/) ending up in
#      production builds.

# ── Build caches ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.cache/
node_modules/.cache/
.expo/
.turbo/
.next/
.maestro-cache/

# ── Replit shell clutter (the workspace root has all of these) ─────
.local/
.config/
.npm/
.dotslash-cache/
.sudo_motd
.eas-tmp/

# ── Replit project config (don't ship to mobile build) ─────────────
.replit
replit.nix
.fork-config.json

# ── Editor + tooling state ──────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.claude.json
.agents/
.lefthook/
.mstack/
.github/

# ── OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
